{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q421323","formula":"C₂H₃BrO₂","hill":"C2H3BrO2","elements":["H","C","O","Br"],"composition":{"C":2.0,"H":3.0,"O":2.0,"Br":1.0},"names":{"en":"Bromoacetic acid","uk":"Бромоцтова кислота"},"descriptions":{"en":"Bromoacetic acid is a chemical compound with the formula BrCH2CO2H. This colorless solid is a relatively strong alkylating agent. Bromoacetic acid and its esters are widely used building blocks in organic synthesis, for example, in pharmaceutical chemistry. The compound is prepared by bromination of acetic acid, such as by a Hell–Volhard–Zelinsky reaction or using other reagents.","uk":"Бромоцтова кислота — це органічна сполука з хімічною формулою CH2BrCO2H. Вона є похідною оцтової кислоти, в якій атом водню метильної групи заміщений на атом брому. Бромоцтова кислота безбарвна тверда речовина, відносно сильний алкілуючий агент, широко використовується в органічному синтезі."},"fame":24,"pubchemCid":6227,"mass":138.95,"charge":0,"smiles":"C(C(=O)O)Br","inchikey":"KDPAWGWELVVRCH-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"2-bromoacetic acid","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"6227","atoms":8,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":2.189,"y":-0.073,"z":0.229,"el":"Br"},{"x":-1.719,"y":0.584,"z":0.235,"el":"O"},{"x":-0.484,"y":-1.293,"z":-0.106,"el":"O"},{"x":0.58,"y":0.855,"z":-0.306,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.566,"y":-0.073,"z":-0.051,"el":"C"},{"x":0.65,"y":1.108,"z":-1.365,"el":"H"},{"x":0.511,"y":1.749,"z":0.317,"el":"H"},{"x":-2.463,"y":-0.036,"z":0.393,"el":"H"}],"bonds":[[0,3,1],[1,4,1],[1,7,1],[2,4,2],[3,4,1],[3,5,1],[3,6,1]]},"sources":[{"role":"identity","name":"Wikidata","url":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q421323","license":"CC0 1.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (en)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bromoacetic_acid","license":"C